{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Cast.Lemmas","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality.qweighted_matches_any_single_level","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality.qweighted_matches_any_single_level","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality.lean#L82-L91","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality.mubar_common_weight_refuted","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality.mubar_common_weight_refuted","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality.lean#L60-L68","doc":"**Refutation.** If some measured `channel m` is not an integer multiple of\n`channel 2`, no common-weight integer-count μ̄-idempotent model (normalised at the\n`m = 2` unit) can reproduce it. The hypothesis `hnonmult` is the empirical input\n(the probe: ¹⁵N/¹¹B = 1.22, ¹⁹F/¹¹B = 0.35 are not integers). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality.mubar_common_weight_forces_integer_multiple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality.mubar_common_weight_forces_integer_multiple","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality.lean#L51-L58","doc":"**With the `m = 2` triple as the unit (`S 2 = 1`), every value is an integer\nmultiple of `channel 2`.** This is the normalisation used by the probe (the single\nBorromean triple at `m = 2` is one μ̄ unit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality.mubar_common_weight_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality.mubar_common_weight_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/MixedMultibondMuBarIntegrality.lean#L38-L49","doc":"**Common-weight models put the channel into integer proportion.** If\n`channel m = w · (S m)` with an integer count `S`, then for all `m, k`\n\n  `channel m · (S k) = channel k · (S m)`\n\n(cross-multiplication) — the values are in the integer ratio `S m : S k`,\nindependent of the common weight `w`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}